course: dictionary
lesson: 7448
title: Pondweed and the bubbles of light
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Pondweed is a plant that grows in ponds and slow rivers, often under or on the water, with green leaves or stems. Scientists use it to learn how plants make their food. «Put a pondweed leaf in a glass of water on a sunny windowsill and watch: tiny bubbles of oxygen rise from it.»
explain: Plants need light to make food. «Water plants use light to make sugar and give off oxygen, so pondweed makes bubbles in sunlight and stops in the dark.» The bubbles are the oxygen escaping, so counting them tells you how hard the plant is working.
explain: Pondweed is also useful to pond life. It gives food, shelter and oxygen to animals like tadpoles and snails. In stories, a pond may be described as «covered in pondweed», which tells you the water is slimy and tangly.
fact: Pondweed grows in ponds and slow rivers.
fact: Pondweed is often a green plant that grows under or on the water.
fact: Canadian pondweed is a common type used in school experiments.
fact: Plants use light to make sugar, and they give off oxygen as they do it. This is called photosynthesis.
fact: Pondweed gives food, shelter and oxygen to pond animals such as tadpoles and snails.
exercise: Where does pondweed grow? | Salt mines under the ground | Tall trees in forests | *Ponds and slow rivers | Deserts and sand dunes
exercise: When does pondweed make oxygen bubbles? | In the dark, at night | *In sunlight | Only when it is cut and dry | When the water is frozen solid
exercise: Which pond animals does pondweed help? | Camels and lizards | *Tadpoles and snails | Eagles and bears | Dolphins and whales
test: In a pondweed experiment, what do you count? | Seeds | Leaves | *Oxygen bubbles | Roots
test: In a story, which words best describe pondweed? | *Slimy and tangly | Hard as stone | Hot and dusty | Shiny and dry
exam: Why does pondweed stop making bubbles in the dark? | It turns into stone at night | *It needs light to make sugar and give off oxygen | It goes to sleep like an animal | The water gets too cold for bubbles
